--TEST--
A closure whose expression body is a call to a `void` method compiles and runs the call, called directly, captured over an outer value and handed to `Core\Script::onExit` — `rule:types/closure-literal`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The expression body is an implicit `return`, and a `void` call has no value
// to return, so the closure returns nothing and the call still runs.
final class Log {
    public static function write(string $line): void {
        echo "log: ", $line, "\n";
    }
}

var $direct = fn (): void => Log::write("direct");
$direct();

// Captured: the body reads an outer value before the call.
string $order = "1042";
var $captured = fn (): void => Log::write("order " . $order);
$captured();

// Handed to a member that takes a callable, and called at the end of the script.
Core\Script::onExit(fn (): void => Log::write("at the end"));
echo "the last line\n";
--EXPECT--
log: direct
log: order 1042
the last line
log: at the end
